auth-client is the Phase 2 browser UI for auth-server (apps/auth-server, port 62000) — React 19 + Vite 8 + @vitejs/plugin-react-swc, dev port 62080, structurally mirroring apps/mud-builder-client (same scaffold shape, no react-router — mud-builder-client has none either, so the whole app switches views on plain useState). It never manages its own auth tokens: every API call uses fetch(..., {credentials:'include'}) and lets the browser hold the httpOnly sa_session cookie auth-server sets; the one exception is API-key tokens from POST /api/keys, which ARE shown to the user (show-once, per auth-server's own design) purely for them to copy elsewhere. The whole app is one state machine driven by useAuthSession()'s status (loading|loggedOut|mustChangePassword|ready) — App.tsx switches between the public flows (login/signup/forgot-password), a blocking forced-password-change screen, and the logged-in shell (account + keys pages) purely off that value. Deployed at https://auth.shatteredarchive.dev alongside auth-server, split the same way build.shatteredarchive.dev is (nginx routes /api/ and /health to auth-server, everything else to this client's nginx-served SPA — see deploy/auth-client.Dockerfile and the auth.shatteredarchive.dev block in deploy/nginx/edge-subdomains.conf).
